      "prompt": "How the reference pictures align with the target video — \u003cPicture 1\u003e (from [Shot 1]) aligns with the 5.17-second mark of the target video.\n\nintegrated_multimodal_description: [Shot 1] Live-action, cinematic, The shot opens in a darkened showroom, with the black sports car held deep in shadow at the rear of the open floor. The surrounding space is sparse and quiet: a broad showroom floor stretches toward the foreground, its empty surface giving the car a clear path forward. Only the car's dark silhouette and the faint sheen along its carbon-fibre body are readable at first, and the contrast makes the vehicle seem to emerge gradually rather than appear all at once. The showroom floor remains empty around it, with no other vehicles or figures visible, so the car's slow advance carries the whole visual change.As the seconds pass, the car begins to pull forward out of the dark. Its nose breaks into the light first, then the long body follows, the carbon-fibre panels picking up a cool, steady reflection as they cross from shadow into the lit portion of the showroom. The movement is slow and controlled, with the car advancing in a straight line while the surrounding floor remains open and uncluttered. The lighting keeps the background subdued and concentrates attention on the car's gradual reveal, letting the glossy dark body separate from the shadow without any sudden change in the room's layout.Near the end, the car eases fully into the foreground light and settles into the wide showroom composition. The full supplied frame is preserved at the final anchor: the same empty showroom setting, the same black sports car with its carbon-fibre body, and the same overall layout and subject placement remain intact. The dark background recedes behind the now-lit vehicle, and the shot resolves with the car occupying the anchored position, completing the requested move from shadow into the open showroom light. At 00:00.000, The black sports car waits deep in shadow at the rear of the empty showroom floor. At 00:00.000, A low engine ignition catches and settles into an idle. At 00:00.000, A faint room ambience fills the empty showroom. At 00:01.400, The car begins to creep forward, its nose crossing from shadow into the light. At 00:01.400, Soft tyre roll moves across the showroom floor. At 00:03.000, The carbon-fibre body slides into the lit foreground, reflections running along its panels. At 00:03.000, The engine holds a steady low idle. At 00:04.600, The car eases into the anchored showroom composition. At 00:04.800, The full supplied frame is matched at the final anchor, with the black sports car settled in the lit showroom. At 00:05.000, The tyre roll fades, leaving the low idle and faint ambience. The camera holds a static shot. Throughout the target video: Do not add spoken or sung lines.\n\noverall_soundscape: Low engine ignition and idle; soft tyre roll across the showroom floor; faint room ambience.\n\nnon_diegetic_music: N/A\n",
